  "worked_solution": "We want to express the area $A$ between the function $f(x)={x}^{2}-2x+2$ and the $x$-axis, between $x=0$ and $x=3.$\n\nThis can be expressed as the definite integral of $f(x)={x}^{2}-2x+2$ between the lower limit $x=0$ and the upper limit $x=3,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{2}-2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
